First of all, I would like to convey that the chakra I am referring to here does not necessarily present the concept of Chakra taken purely from Indian tradition; rather, I am trying to position this concept of chakra as one of humanity's efforts to understand the human self. Just as in modern times we have neuroscience, molecular biology, neurology, and so on. From a research perspective, some aspects of the chakra concept might be wrong, in addition to certainly having aspects that are right—much like an expert conducting research or formulating a theory, where parts of that theory might turn out to be incorrect, or it could also be entirely true. That is how I view the concept of chakra.
